findings.body:
Returning `"Access-Control-Allow-Origin": origin ?? "*"` together with `"Access-Control-Allow-Credentials": "true"` violates the CORS spec. When credentials are used the browser requires an exact origin match; `*` is rejected and a reflected arbitrary origin enables reflected-origin attacks.

```suggestion
  if (!origin) {
    return {};
  }
  return {
    "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": origin,
    "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials": "true",
    Vary: "Origin",
  };
```
